cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the paper as below."
title: "Joint Radio-Environment Map Construction for THz ISAC via Conditional Flow Matching"
abstract: >-
  Terahertz (THz) integrated sensing and communication (ISAC) requires accurate
  radio-environment awareness despite severe blockage and sparse measurements.
  This paper investigates joint reconstruction of received signal strength (RSS)
  maps and obstacle occupancy grids from sparse RSS samples, formulated as
  conditional generation of a two-channel radio-environment map. A conditional
  flow matching framework transports Gaussian noise to the conditional map
  distribution, guided by sparse RSS observations and sensing masks, and jointly
  reconstructs RSS fields and obstacle occupancy through one-step or few-step ODE
  sampling. Ray-tracing experiments show lower MSE than DDPM, DDNM, and
  RadioUNet across the tested sensing ratios.
